            <sparkle:shortVersionString>0.83</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <description><![CDATA[<style>
  body { font-family: -apple-system, sans-serif; font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.5; padding: 12px; }
  h3 { margin: 0 0 8px; font-size: 14px; }
  h2 { margin: 0 0 8px; font-size: 12px; }
  ul { margin: 4px 0; padding-left: 20px; }
  li { margin: 2px 0; }
</style>
<h3>What's New</h3>
<h2>New Features</h2>
<ul>
<li>Typing something that isn&#x27;t a web address into the browser pane&#x27;s URL bar now searches Google, like Safari and Chrome. For example, &quot;swift async let&quot; or &quot;hello&quot; opens search results.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Improvements</h2>
<ul>
<li>The URL bar now recognizes more kinds of addresses. Domains such as example.com load over https. Localhost, [::1], IPv4 addresses such as 192.168.1.20, and hostnames with a port such as devbox:8080 load over http. Addresses like about:blank load as typed.</li>
<li>Search terms are encoded safely, so queries such as &quot;c++ &amp; rust?&quot; reach Google intact.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
